WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.257
Double jeopardy says small brands suffer twice.

00:00:03.307 --> 00:00:07.042
They have fewer buyers, and those buyers are slightly less loyal.

00:00:07.092 --> 00:00:09.826
So growth comes from penetration.

00:00:10.533 --> 00:00:12.134
Watch the cola fridge.

00:00:12.184 --> 00:00:13.962
Coke buyers stream past.

00:00:14.012 --> 00:00:15.448
Pepsi gets fewer of them,

00:00:15.498 --> 00:00:18.443
and even its own buyers often grab a Coke.

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:21.465
So a Pepsi loyalty app hits a ceiling.

00:00:21.515 --> 00:00:26.323
The answer is broad reach and wider availability, to recruit light buyers.

00:00:27.033 --> 00:00:28.221
Use it like this:

00:00:28.271 --> 00:00:29.071
when a plan bets on loyalty,

00:00:28.413 --> 00:00:29.213
argue for reach instead.

00:00:29.085 --> 00:00:33.975
Loyalty follows share.
